1. The run's abort signal reaches every Mistral request: the raw stream
   fetch and structuredOutput's chat.complete (ai-mistral 0.6.11 on
   upstream main has neither). Upstream PR to be opened; remove when released.
2. A non-OK response's error carries its HTTP status and parsed body, and the
   RUN_ERROR forwards them as rawEvent, as the SDK-based adapters do since
   TanStack/ai#985. The rethrow after RUN_ERROR is upstream's (tested) and
   stays. Upstream PR to be opened; remove when released.
3. The terminal event carries the choice's finish_reason as
   metadata.providerStopReason (null when the stream ended without one), so the
   service decides every finish reason (model_length and error included) from
   the SDK's union (apps/api/src/lib/chat/provider-stop-reasons.ts). Remove
   when upstream exposes the raw reason.

